    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="1147" n="1137" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg1137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.414/4–645: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Representatives </hi><anchor n="18" xml:id="d855-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-06T08:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1945—8
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The unilateral procedure outlined in Deptelcirc March 31, 3 p.m. does not apply
                    in countries to which you are accredited and reference was for your information
                    only. However, you should keep the Department informed of any disposition made
                    of such records by the countries to which you are accredited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d855-f1" n="18" type="source" xml:id="d855-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to all American diplomatic representatives except those at Madrid, Lisbon,
                    Bern, Stockholm, Dublin, Vatican City, and Kabul.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
